{
  "frames": [
    {
      "frame_number": 1,
      "caption": "The landlord told me his house was full, and I agreed, rather than wander further on so bitter a night, to share a harpooneer\u2019s blanket if he were not decidedly objectionable.",
      "caption_zone": "bottom_left",
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/generated_frames/frame_001.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/lettered_frames/frame_001.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 2,
      "caption": "My misgivings grew; I changed my mind about that harpooneer and tried the bench for a bed, till the knots, planes, and freezing draughts beat me off the plan.",
      "caption_zone": "top_right",
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/generated_frames/frame_002.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/lettered_frames/frame_002.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 3,
      "caption": "Close upon midnight I made the landlord speak out, learned the talk of 'selling his head' meant \u2019balmed New Zealand heads, and yet let him lead me up to the prodigious bed.",
      "caption_zone": "bottom_center",
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/generated_frames/frame_003.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/lettered_frames/frame_003.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 4,
      "caption": "Alone, I examined the harpooneer\u2019s outlandish gear, even tried on his shaggy door-mat poncho, then, thinking he would not come, blew out the light and turned in.",
      "caption_zone": "top_left",
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/generated_frames/frame_004.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/lettered_frames/frame_004.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1586,
        "y2": 992
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 5,
      "caption": "Presently he entered with a New Zealand head, prayed to his little wooden idol, stripped to his tattooings, and at last sprang into bed with his tomahawk-pipe, whereat I sang out.",
      "caption_zone": "top_center",
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/generated_frames/frame_005.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/lettered_frames/frame_005.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 6,
      "caption": "When the landlord burst in and named him Queequeg, I chose to trust the sober cannibal if he stowed his pipe, and turning in again I never slept better in my life.",
      "caption_zone": "bottom_right",
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/generated_frames/frame_006.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_auto/chapter_003/lettered_frames/frame_006.png",
      "frame_box": {
